>
  <section>
    <h2>Why Finova exists</h2>
    <p>Important money questions often begin with a simple number: a monthly EMI, projected maturity value, take-home salary or estimated tax. The arithmetic may be standard, but the result is difficult to trust when the formula, assumptions and limitations are hidden.</p>
    <p>Finova brings the inputs, result, breakdown and explanation together in one calm interface.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the platform provides</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Calculators for loans, investing, salary, payroll and tax estimates.</li>
      <li>Indian rupee formatting with lakh and crore grouping.</li>
      <li>Breakdowns, charts and schedules where they improve understanding.</li>
      <li>Plain-English guides connected to relevant calculators.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who it is designed for</h2>
    <p>Finova is built primarily for people in India who want a quick estimate without creating an account, navigating a product-sales flow or decoding unnecessary financial jargon.</p>
    <p>The calculators are general tools. They are not tailored recommendations and do not know a user’s full financial circumstances.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How the calculators work</h2>
    <p>The current calculator engines run in the browser. Financial mathematics is separated from the interface, and automated tests cover normal and edge cases. Each calculator identifies its formula or methodology and displays important assumptions.</p>
    <p>Rule-sensitive calculators keep changing parameters in identifiable configuration rather than scattering them through interface code. Read more on the <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How Finova approaches transparency</h2>
    <p>Calculated values, estimates, projections and statutory assumptions are labelled differently. When a rule or rate can change, the interface uses an applicable year, editable assumption or source reference where one is available.</p>
    <p>Finova does not use testimonials, user counts, ratings or authority claims to make a result appear more reliable than the underlying calculation.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Finova does not provide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Personal financial, investment, tax, legal or accounting advice.</li>
      <li>Banking, brokerage, lending, tax filing or account-management services.</li>
      <li>Guaranteed investment returns, loan approvals or statutory entitlements.</li>
      <li>Recommendations for a financial product or provider.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Start with the <a href="/calculators">calculator directory</a>, read the <a href="/guides">guides</a>, or review the <a href="/disclaimer">financial disclaimer</a>.</p>
  </section>
</StaticPageLayout>
